WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.140
so there's some, uh, pretty bad news for Bernie
Sanders in a recent poll, which says that

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.460
Ernie support among young voters has dropped
significantly.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.290
Now, I hate that I have to do this sometimes
multiple times in one show, but as a reminder,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.740
I am just the messenger here.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.740
Okay?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.740
I didn't do this poll.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.740
I'm not anti Bernie.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.740
I like Bernie.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.230
He's one of my top candidates for 2020.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.750
I voted for him in the 2016 primary.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:28.940
I'm telling you the news, which is what this
poll is asserting, I am not the person that

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.090
you should attack simply for telling you that
this is a poll that has been released.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.420
Now these numbers are from a new morning consult
poll.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:42.570
Bernie has been super strong in the 18 to
29 age bracket and in the same pole, morning

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:50.190
consult back in February, Bernie had support
from 46% of those age 18 to 29 in March, almost

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.190
the same.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:55.280
He still had 45% of 18 to 29 year olds supporting
him.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.899
This number has now dropped to 33% in May.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:02.620
That's a reduction of more than 25% in the
support from young people.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:09.650
So the obvious question is who is that 18
to 29 year old cohort, but moving towards

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.720
in the 2020 Democratic primary?

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.430
And the answer is maybe surprising to some
in our audience because a bunch of that support

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:21.910
has moved over to Joe Biden and I know many
in our audience will say and have been saying,

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:26.920
David, only old people are supporting Joe
Biden.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.770
And it's true that Joe Biden has disproportionate
support from older voters, but according to

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:38.160
this poll, Joe Biden has gone from under 20%
support from 18 to 29 year olds, 29 year olds,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.890
up to 24% in the latest survey.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.390
Elizabeth Warren has also increased her support.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:51.610
She's gone from around 5% support from 18
to 29 year olds in March up to more like 10%

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.610
now.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:57.670
And that's the majority or a significant portion
rather have the support that Bernie has lost

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:58.800
from that age group.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.970
So let's go through it.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:05.250
First of all, are there any glaring methodology
issues which would suggest that the poll results

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.520
are just completely wrong?

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.140
Nothing obvious that I was able to find when
I looked at it.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:16.569
The next question is, will it matter if there's
been a shift in 18 to 29 year old support

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.920
from Bernie to Warren and from Bernie to Biden?

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.569
If 18 to 29 year olds don't show up to vote.

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:27.650
And what I mean by that is that historically
older voters are much more reliable voters,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:32.530
whereas young voters are less likely to vote
once election day actually arrives.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:39.469
And once we think about that, we have to ask
why is it that some of the 18 to 29 year olds

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:44.790
who were supporting Bernie Sanders a month
ago, two months ago, why have they moved on

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.079
to someone else?

00:02:46.079 --> 00:02:49.780
And why would it be Biden and why would it
be Elizabeth Warren?

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:56.140
Uh, when it comes to Biden, it's not likely
to be over Biden's politics specifically.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.879
I mean, Biden is very moderate.

00:02:57.879 --> 00:03:02.189
He is very much in the line of Hillary Clinton.

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:08.519
Not drastically different from, you know,
a 1970s moderate Republican in many ways,

00:03:08.519 --> 00:03:13.739
but I think it's undeniable that Biden's perceived
association with the Obama Presidency around

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:19.170
which people on the older end of 18 to 29
may remember positively and have some nostalgia

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.349
for particularly when you look at who's in
the White House right now.

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:28.700
Um, when it comes to some of that Bernie 18
to 29 year olds support shifting to Elizabeth

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.700
Warren.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.330
There is a contingent that liked Elizabeth
Warren in 2016 but ended up with Bernie as

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:38.969
sort of the closest person to Warren that
they actually had a chance to vote for, uh,

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:40.849
during the 2016 primary.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:45.109
They may simply be reinvigorated by the fact
that Elizabeth Warren's campaign is getting

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:47.050
more attention in the last four to six weeks.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.239
It's been picking up some polling steam.

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:53.000
And my message if want Bernie to win, is very
simple.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.499
Don't react to this story by don't, don't
react by attacking me because that will do

00:03:57.499 --> 00:03:59.709
nothing to help Bernie Sanders win.

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:03.309
Um, don't react by attacking Joe Biden or
whoever.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:08.999
Go and volunteer for Bernie's campaign and
make the case to people who are already on

00:04:08.999 --> 00:04:13.799
the left that you believe Bernie is their
best, their best option from those that are

00:04:13.799 --> 00:04:14.919
available.

00:04:14.919 --> 00:04:21.240
Remember that a spirited primary, uh, healthy,
uh, disagreement within the primary, it's

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.360
not a bad thing even if Bernie Sanders is
losing support.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:31.110
Because my guess is that in the end, most
Warren supporters, if Bernie's the nominee

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.710
are going to vote for Bernie.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.710
Okay.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:39.600
Most Bernie supporters, if Warren is the nominee,
are going to vote for Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.849
Whether they all would vote for Joe Biden
if Biden's the nominee.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:48.139
I'm a little bit more concerned about, but
the point is, it's okay for the progressive

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:50.110
contingent to be sort of divided.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.879
At this point in time we've seen as I predicted
would happen as soon as Joe Biden announced

00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:58.550
his candidacy, the establishment support has
coalesced around him.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.900
So Beto has been dropping.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:08.280
Cory Booker has been dropping and that establishment
centrist wing has been seriously just joining

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.500
Joe Biden effectively.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.500
And that's why his poll numbers are doing
well.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.629
The progressive vote is still very much more
split between candidates and it doesn't really

00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:20.409
necessarily tell us what it is that's going
to happen once the Democratic primary is settled.

00:05:20.409 --> 00:05:25.620
I think most of those voters who now are split
are going to come over to the democratic,

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.000
uh, a nominee almost, no matter who it is.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.720
I will put it that way and maybe we'll dig
into what I mean by that.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.210
Uh, on an upcoming show,

